  "worked_solution": "First, we find the two numbers in the table that $0.1700$ lies between. These numbers are $0.1685$ and $0.1711.$ So, we have the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.1685 & <0.1700<0.1711\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above inequality in terms of $\u03a6,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u03a6(-0.96) & <\u03a6(z)<\u03a6(-0.95).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, using interval bisection, we can approximate $z$ as\n\n$$\nz\u2248\\frac{-0.96+(-0.95)}{2}=-0.955.\n$$",
